Goal is to create a game focus on teaching and practicing the fundamentals of Linux
Two options to decide between at this point: 
1) Fighting Game 
- have a tutorial to teach the Linux and how to play
- a beginner mode to start practicing and further teach Linux
- intermediate and hard modes to up difficulty/change recall type 
- regular fights and boss battles with different ways to "fight" them
- inherently only single player

2) Racing Game
- have a tutorial to explain how to play
- teach Linux commands in beginner mode
- practice usage in race mode
- race against computer levels (easy, med, hard), a friend, or yourself (based on score)
- questions give more or less movement based on question difficulty (could ask question and allow user to choose how they want to answer - full recall (no multi choice), 4 option multi choice, 2 option multi choice, etc)

I think the fighting game would be much more fun tbh 
but the racing game would allow the user to play with others

DECISIONS
- Create the Racing Game. It will be easier to program to start, and I can always create the fighting game later
- have multiple maps for different difficulties
- have visible scoring mechanism
- have a learning mode and a coding mode
-- learning mode should:
--- encourage the student to use their CLI to test out prompts before answering
--- be multiple choice 
--- not be timed
-- coding mode should:
--- prompt the student with the answers from learning mode
--- have the student respond with the command they were originally prompted with in learning mode
--- have a timing function (think Kahoot - faster answers = more points, but only if they are correct)
--- give 3 chances for student to answer correctly before giving the answer and prompting them for the next question
--- if more than one command could work as the answer, accept any of the potential responses as correct
- have a race your friends mode (local multiplayer; one device)
-- players take turns answering the same question and get points based on who answered faster
-- compatible with coding mode

